2. CANONICAL EVENT MODEL
==================================================

Create/strengthen a canonical typed MemoryEvent model.

Every event should have stable metadata where appropriate:

- eventId
- eventType
- timestamp
- memoryId when applicable
- actorId when applicable
- actorType when applicable
- organizationId when applicable
- workspaceId when applicable
- projectId when applicable
- requestId/correlationId when available
- previousState when applicable
- newState when applicable
- version when applicable
- source/service
- severity/category
- sanitized metadata

Use existing naming conventions if they differ.

Do not break existing consumers.

==================================================
3. EVENT TYPES
==================================================

Audit the existing event types.

Ensure the event system can represent the existing lifecycle/security/
memory operations.

At minimum support existing concepts such as:

